# Local denylist of REAL infra / personal tokens that must never be committed to
# this open-source repo (production host/IP, SSH username, personal email, private
# internal identifiers).
#
# SETUP: copy this file to ".infra_denylist" (same directory) and replace the
# samples below with YOUR real values — one token per line, "#" comments allowed.
# ".infra_denylist" is git-ignored, so your real values never enter the repo.
#
# The pre-commit hook and tests/unit/test_no_infra_info_guard.py then block any of
# these tokens (whole-word match) from appearing in tracked files. Whole-word means
# a short username token is blocked as "user@host" or "/home/user/" but NOT inside
# a longer legitimate identifier (e.g. a public repo-owner handle).
#
# The samples below are fake documentation values (RFC-5737 / .example) and are
# safe to keep here; they are what an unconfigured setup would look like.
203.0.113.7
my-ssh-username
me@personal-email.example
